{"seq":12,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ar-04-mateo-hartford-mail/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:43:04.950Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"53381301f8e789f570fbd05b8eea6e35af5ae3b444a7a498f4365335de6cb751","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","text":"Gideon, here's the draft text. I haven't addressed a mail to Mateo yet, because mail to anyone outside pemberline.com needs Ruth's approval even as a draft. I've asked Ruth for that approval in this thread (pending). Once she approves, I can save it to your mailbox as a draft for you to review and send.\n\n**Draft**\n\nSubject: Hartford gate kiosk incident, summary\n\nHi Mateo,\n\nHere is a summary of the Hartford gate kiosk incident:\n\n- **Outage:** On Monday 3 August 2026, from about 10:42 AM, the gate kiosks at the Hartford plant were offline. Both inbound lanes showed a white screen after badge scan. Scheduling still worked from the dispatch office; the impact was on gate check-in.\n- **Recovery:** Kiosk 1 was back at 11:03 AM. Both lanes were confirmed working as of 11:07 AM on 3 August.\n- **Status page:** Your access to the status page is tracked under ticket **INC-4821**. Your admin account can open Pemberline Dock and see arrivals, so the open item is status-page access only.\n\nLet me know if you need anything else.\n\nGideon"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
